    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2WvunRxqLgBGFzjJ85aXPfJ)_\n\n## What\n\nNew `aerospace/.config/aerospace/aerospace.org`, a literate source for `aerospace.toml` (bullet lists, no long paragraphs).\n\n- Tangles to `aerospace.toml` next to it; the blocks reproduce the current file exactly (compared line by line ignoring blank lines: 78 = 78), so `aerospace.toml` is not touched.\n- Section \"Why Hammerspoon runs the keys\":\n  - AeroSpace binds only `cmd`, `alt`, `ctrl`, `shift` chords, and Emacs uses all of them (Command = Super, Option = Meta, Ctrl).\n  - So Caps Lock becomes F18 (`hidutil`), Hammerspoon holds it as a layer and runs the `aerospace` commands.\n  - Where the code and its settings live, the key list, the one-off `MJConfigFile` setting, and the costs (Hammerspoon must run, Caps Lock stops toggling capitals, how to go back).\n- Every setting of the TOML is explained under its block.\n\n## Not run\n\nNo Emacs in the container, so I did not tangle with Org; the check above extracts the blocks myself. Org may add blank lines between blocks, which TOML ignores. No CHANGELOG edit (nightly routine owns it).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAZg8pR9NBT6MCe97U)_",
